msgid "The rST text."
msgstr ""
".. _Introduction:\n"
"Introduction\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
".. warning::\n"
"    *Some* words and phrases may not be accurately translated.\n"
"\n"
"Welcome to My Project\n"
"--------------------\n"
"\n"
"My Project\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"### What is My Project?\n"
"\n"
"My Project is a great tool for doing things.\n"
"### What can you do with My Project?\n"
"\n"
"You can use My Project for various tasks."

#: of readme_rosetta.sphinx_handler.SphinxHandler.fix_rst_underlines:4
msgid "The rST text with fixed underlines."
msgstr ""
".. _underlines:\n"
"\n"
"Fixed Underlines\n"
"================\n"
"\n"
"A fixed underline is a typographical feature used to draw attention to specific parts of the text.\n"
"\n"
"### How to Create a Fixed Underline\n"
"\n"
"To create a fixed underline, surround the desired text with `<u>` and `</u>` tags.\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"*This is some text with an underlined section:* \n"
"<u>underlined text here</u>\n"
"\n"
"*This is some regular text.*\n"
"\n"
"Fixed Underlines\n"
"----------------\n"
"\n"
"The use of fixed underlines is largely considered obsolete in modern typography, as they can be difficult to read and do not provide a clear visual distinction from surrounding text."

